<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of the Republic of China</h1><p class="st-meta">1937 CE – 1940 CE · capital Beijing</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first major Chinese collaborationist regime of the Sino-Japanese War, set up in Beijing in 1937 to govern occupied northern China.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugou-bridge">Marco Polo Bridge</a> incident of July 1937, the Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china">North China</a> Area Army occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianjin">Tianjin</a> and pushed south. On 14 December 1937, the day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> fell, it installed the Provisional Government of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China</a> in Beijing, headed by the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-government">Beiyang</a> finance minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-kemin">Wang Kemin</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime claimed to govern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> under the old five-coloured flag of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a>, though Japanese advisers controlled policy and much of the countryside was held by Communist and Nationalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>. It founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinmin-hui">Xinmin Hui</a>, a mass organisation promoting cooperation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and absorbed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/east-hebei-autonomous-government">East Hebei Autonomous Government</a> in 1938.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In March 1940 it was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/wang-jingwei-regime">Wang Jingwei regime</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, continuing as the semi-autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china">North China</a> Political Council until 1945. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-kemin">Wang Kemin</a> was arrested after the war and died in prison in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1937 CE – 1940 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.25%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1937 CE – 1940 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beijing</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wang Kemin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandarin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Peking Provisional Government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1938&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-the-republic-of-china" aria-label="Provisional Government of the Republic of China on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7548 750 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of the Republic of China lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7868 1006L7879 1009M7868 1006L8529 1145M7868 1006L8056 1267"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7879 1009h0M8529 1145h0M8056 1267h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7868 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7868 1006h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The d